From 531c82322f76f3f6d1c537d7351f96567264eb47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omarchy Authors <omarchy@omarchy.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:49:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15: Load the Purwa
 Iris firmware

The X1P-42-100 iris node requests qcvss8380.mbn. ASUS signs that image
only for the X Elite (SoC hw id 0xa009). On the X1P42100 (0xa016)
TrustZone rejects it from qcom_pas_init_image with -EINVAL, and the
video decoder never probes.

The production image in the same Windows package is qcvss8380_pa.mbn
(vfw-3.1:rel0088, IMAGE_VARIANT_STRING=PROD_IRIS3_1P), signed for
0xa016. The other X1P42100 boards already load that name: the Dell
Inspiron 14 Plus 5441, the Galaxy Book4 Edge 15, the IdeaPad Slim 3x
and the IdeaPad 5x 2-in-1.

Point this node at qcvss8380_pa.mbn. Installing that file where the
previous tree looked made iris bind /dev/video0 and mpv decode H.264
with v4l2m2m-copy.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts
index c754104..845b7ef 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 };
 
 &iris {
-	firmware-name = "qcom/x1p42100/ASUSTeK/vivobook-s15/qcvss8380.mbn";
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1p42100/ASUSTeK/vivobook-s15/qcvss8380_pa.mbn";
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
